              <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-3">
                Searching this website
              </h4>
              <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
                Search runs entirely inside your browser. When you load the directory, your browser
                downloads an index of all our programs and searches that copy locally. What you type
                into the search box is never sent to us or to anyone else — there is no search
                server to send it to.
              </p>

              <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3">
                Carl in the mobile and desktop apps
              </h4>
              <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
                In the iPhone, iPad and Mac apps, Carl runs on your device using Apple Intelligence,
                with a copy of our directory stored on the device itself.
              </p>
              <ul class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 space-y-2 mb-4 list-disc pl-5">
                <li>
                  <strong>Your questions stay on your device.</strong> Nothing you ask Carl is sent to
                  us, because there is nowhere to send it.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>It works offline.</strong> No signal is needed, which also means Carl works
                  in places where using it is nobody else's business.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>Nothing is used for training.</strong> Apple's on-device model does not learn
                  from what you ask it, and we never see it.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>On devices without Apple Intelligence,</strong> Carl falls back to searching
                  the copy of the directory stored on your device. Still no network, still nothing sent.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3">
                Using Carl inside another company's AI chatbot
              </h4>
              <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
                You can now connect Carl to an AI assistant you already use, such as ChatGPT or
                Claude, through what is called an MCP server. <strong
                  >If you do this, please read this section carefully</strong
                > — it is the one situation where your questions reach a company other than us.
              </p>
              <ul class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 space-y-2 mb-4 list-disc pl-5">
                <li>
                  <strong>Your conversation belongs to that chatbot's provider, not us.</strong> Whatever
                  you type goes to OpenAI, Anthropic, or whoever makes the assistant you chose, and is
                  handled under their privacy policy. We have no visibility into it and no control over
                  it.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>What our server receives:</strong> only the search terms that assistant decides
                  to look up — for example "food bank Oakland". Not your name, not your account, not the
                  rest of your conversation.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>What our server sends back:</strong> public directory entries, the same ones
                  anyone can read on this website.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>What we keep:</strong> nothing. Our MCP server stores no queries and no logs
                  of what was asked. Our hosting provider keeps standard technical logs, described below.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>This is optional and opt-in.</strong> It only happens if you deliberately connect
                  Carl to another assistant. Simply using this website never involves any of it.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3">
                What we shut down, and a correction
              </h4>
              <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
                Until September 16, 2026, complex questions were answered by an AI server we ran
                ourselves. That server has been retired, along with the search server that
                accompanied it. Queries sent to it were processed in memory and never stored, and
                that remains true of everything we no longer hold.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
                <strong>A correction:</strong> earlier versions of this policy said that server ran Meta's
                Llama 3.1 8B model. That was wrong. It actually ran Qwen2.5 3B Instruct, an open-source
                model published by Alibaba. The substance of what we told you was accurate — the model
                ran on our own hardware, your queries were not stored, and nothing was used for training
                — but we named the wrong model, and we would rather say so than quietly delete it.
              </p>

              <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3">
                Simple Language Feature
              </h4>
              <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
                Bay Navigator's optional "Simple Language" accessibility feature shows a version of
                our text written to about an 8th-grade reading level. The simplified wording is
                written ahead of time and ships with the site as ordinary page content. This
                feature:
              </p>
              <ul class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 space-y-2 mb-4 list-disc pl-5">
                <li>
                  <strong>Is pre-generated, not live:</strong> the simplified text is produced when Bay
                  Tides publishes a site update, and then shipped as part of the page. Turning the feature
                  on sends no request anywhere.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>Collects no personal data:</strong> because nothing is generated on demand,
                  no user or device identifier, location, or other personal information is involved.
                </li>
                <li>
